                **      22 Jan 85  MSA  Add IWM reconfigure for //c version      **      23 Jan 85  MSA  Move Comm routines to $C800 ($C900)      **                      Fixed zero page preservation             ** ***  23 Jan 85  MSA  RELEASE VERSION 0.03 (Apple)             **      25 Jan 85  MSA  Swap slot dep read and boot code (//c)   **                      Add other //c differences...             **      30 Jan 85  MSA  Add auxtype byte                         **                      Fix comm error on receive packet         **                      Fix checksum to include MSBs of overhead **      07 Feb 85  MSA  Add COUT support on boot fail            ** ***  08 Feb 85  MSA  RELEASE VERSION 1.00A (alpha)            **      22 Feb 85  MSA  Add bytecount in X,Y on PC calls         **                      Change hard reset time to 1 ms (was 83)  **                      Crunched code by adding ClrPhases        **                      Add zeroing of third block byte (ProDOS) **      06 Mar 85  MSA  Fixed slot 7 goof (stack screw up)       **                      No clear phases on retries               **                      Hard reset time to 40 ms                 **                      Pass #parms instead of unit# and no chk  **                      Init code (all reset vs. comm reset)     **                      Add 2 bytes to pass a full 9 byte cmd    **      16 Mar 85  MSA  Fix bytecount on retries                 **                      Boot block must be $800=$01, $801<>$00   **      17 Mar 85  MSA  Remove WRREQ while waiting for motor TO  **                      Remove glitch on /ENBL2 in AssignID      **      20 Mar 85  MSA  Add interrupt on/off/poll support        **                      Reset pulse to 80 ms                     **                      //c delay of 100 ms on initial AssignID  **                      ID bytes changed                         **                      Retransmit implemented (RecPack)         **                      Add send data packet retries (5)         **                      Rearrange PC stack adjust                **                      Add //c Appletalk vector                 **      24 Mar 85  MSA  Add //c millisecond wait each call       ** ***  25 Mar 85  MSA  RELEASE VERSION 1.00B (beta) (//e)       **      18 Apr 85  MSA  Clear decimal mode                       **                      Eight bytes are returned on stat unit#0  **                      Stat Unit#0 scode<>0 is rejected         **                      X and Y set to 0008 on status unit#0     **                      Enable interrupts done correctly         **                      Add unit#0 parameter count checking      ** ***  22 Apr 85  MSA  RELEASE VERSION 1.01B                    ** ***  15 May 85  MSA  RELEASE VERSION 1.0                      **      22 Jul 85  MSA  Add Phoenix Motor off patch to //e ver   **                                                               ** ***  16 Sep 85  RBM  Initial Cortland Modifications           **                                                               ** ***  15 Dec 85  RBM  Re-ORG for new rom, and ram              **                                                               ** ***  26 Dec 85  RBM  Delete C500 messages, move tables to     **                      C500 space, DSony.Entry at $4600         **                                                               * * ***  23 Jan 86  RBM  Implemented final PC extension.          **                                                               ** ***  18 Mar 86  RBM  QC-10 fix, Ram/RomDisk parameters.       **                                                               ** ***  26 MAR 86  RBM  BETA 1.0                                 **                                                               ** ***   1 APR 86  RBM  Fixed RAMDISK boot problem.              **                                                               ** ***   2 APR 86  RBM  Fixed PR#5 boot problem when no disk     **                      in device.                               **                                                               ** ---   8 Oct 86  RBM  Reduction of code space in $C5XX.        **                      Fixed PR#5 boot problem with regart to   **                      INTCXROM.  Fixed RESET so that only slot **                      6 motor-on speed detect is disabled.     **                                                               **  01  18 Dec 86  RBM  Fixed parameter organization so that the **                      Read & Write (MAC BLOCK) calls work for  **                      more than just block $000000.            **                                                               **  01  18 Dec 86  RBM  Fixed boot code for PR#5 or PR#6 to save **                      and restore the STATEREG (CXROM).        **                                                               **  01  18 Dec 86  RBM  IWM mode changes now only affect slot 6  **                      motor on detect.  Slot 4 or 7 motor on   **                      will no longer cause packet comm. errors **                                                               **  01  24 Jan 87  RBM  C500 space to set D=$00 to fix disk      **                      copy protection schemes. (they broke     **                      the rules, not us)                       *******************************************************************  03     Aug 88  JOA  Moved zeropage save and interrup off     **                      code before zero page used to extract    **                      SmartPort command byte and parmlist ptr  **                                                               **  03     Sep 88  JOA  Fixed the increment of bank byte bug for **                      Control list pointer after extracting    **                      control list length word.                **                                                               **  03     Sep 88  JOA  Changed C5xx reference to ENTRY so it    **                      enters via a jmp in vector table at the  **                      beginning of SmartPort code so code body **                      can be re-assembled without $C5xx chan'g **                                                               **  03     Sep 88  JOA  Removed AppleDisk3.5 drivers use of the  **                      SmartPort SetMode routine and its vector **                      A3.5 driver has its own mode set routine **                      which is expected to expand for SWIMchip **                                                               **  03     Oct 88  JOA  Added Test&ResetFlag call to SmartPort   **                      to support GS/OS's need to disallow back **                      door access thru Slot 5 firmware. A word **                      is maintained for devs 0,1..14,&up       **                                                               **  03     Nov 88  JOA  Fixed ProDOS Status call error translate **                      so Offline error ($2F) is higher priority**                      than NoWrite error ($2B); This 'bug' was **                      inherited from Rev 01 code.              **                                                               **  03     Nov 88  JOA  Removed code from RamDisk interface that **                      replaced all RamDisk error codes with    **                      I/O ERROR ($27)                          **                                                               **  03     Nov 88  JOA  Added code to call the new Slot Arbiter  **                      to switch slot 6 in/out.                 **                      Also changed OpenWndw to use slot Arbiter**                                                               **  03    July 89  JOA  Added BRA in rom disk dispatcher so that **                      init call will dispatch to the ROM_DISK. **                                                               **  04    May 1991 JOA  Converted to MPW 3.2 and AsmIIGS         ******************************************************************